<section class="how not-content" aria-labelledby="how">
	<h2 id="how">Three steps, no setup</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>
			<span class="number">01</span>
			<h3>Write the file</h3>
			<p>
				Each key is a table, each table a list of rows. Memless reads value types, row ids and
				relations from the data itself: <code>user_id</code> points at <code>users</code>.
			</p>
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="number">02</span>
			<h3>Query it with SQL</h3>
			<p>
				SELECT with WHERE, ORDER BY and one INNER JOIN, COUNT and SUM, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, and
				transactions. Anything else is refused, never approximated.
			</p>
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="number">03</span>
			<h3>Changes go back to the file</h3>
			<p>
				Every accepted write rewrites the file, replaced atomically so a crash never leaves it
				half-written. Transactions write it once, on COMMIT.
			</p>
		</li>
	</ol>
</section>

